// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6030 new: OpenAI Codex sandbox abuse detection rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6030
// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: OpenAI Codex Command Runner Spawned By Unexpected Parent Process
// Sigma ID: e9a4b2c3-8d5f-4e6b-ac9d-2f3e4a5b6c7d
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Jonathan Johnson, Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-05-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1059, T1574
// Description: Detects the OpenAI Codex command runner binary (codex-command-runner-*.exe) being spawned by a
//   process other than codex.exe. The legitimate execution chain is strictly: codex.exe -> codex-
//   command-runner-<version>.exe. Execution via any other parent process may indicate abuse of the
//   command runner binary for sandbox escape, lateral movement, or persistence by an attacker who
//   has obtained access to the Codex installation directory.
// False positives:
//   - Security tooling or EDR agents that wrap process creation may alter the observed parent
// References:
//   - https://jonny-johnson.medium.com/a-deep-dive-into-codex-windows-sandbox-a2489bf4ae91
//   - https://openai.com/index/building-codex-windows-sandbox/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/a20c16d6d3eef0c2c625df9d2ac3e18c1b12187c/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_codex_command_runner_unexpected_parent.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath contains "\\codex-command-runner-" and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\codex.exe"))
